ue>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmdFaultAck</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>696</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmdEnterMaint</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>704</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmdExitMaint</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>712</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSetpointsChanged</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>720</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHmiCommLoss</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ feed into ST_Faults.bHmiCommLoss]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>728</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nLastHeartbeat</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ heartbeat supervision]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>736</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonHbTimeout</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>768</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFirstCycle</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>992</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonUptime</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ uptime]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1024</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nUptimeSeconds</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1248</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbTick</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1280</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_Purge</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 FB_Purge | VERIFIED 8.2.26 DA
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

 MECHANISM - it is a repeating DRAIN / EQUILIBRATE cycle, not a one-shot:
   * A pressure band is built around the target setpoint:
       upper = TSP + band 
       lower = TSP - band 
   * Purge only proceeds while upstream pressure is inside that band.
   * Cycle, gated by "OK to purge" latch:
       1. Open drain valve SV1 for tDrainOpen 
       2. Close SV1, wait tEquilibrate to let water settle and for the boiler
			pressuer loop to raise the upstream pressure to within the range
       3. If the EMPTY switch (LS3) now reads empty -> purge complete.
          Otherwise, if still in band, re-open SV1 and repeat.
   * Overall watchdog: if the cycle runs longer than tPurgeTimeout -> bPurgeFault
   * After complete: water fill is allowed and the state machine advances
     to SetDiffPressure

 Reports intent only:
   qDrainValve -> FB_OutputHandler -> GVL_IO.qxSv1Drain (single writer).
   bPurgeComplete -> FB_StateMachine (S11 -> S13 transition).
   bPurgeTimeout  -> FB_FaultMonitor (latches the fault, like every other).
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>896</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE while state = PurgeVessel]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rUpstreamPress</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ upstream pressure [Torr]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bEmptyFiltered</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ filtered LS3 empty switch]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>qDrainValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ -> FB_OutputHandler -> SV1 drain]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>104</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bPurgeComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ -> state machine]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bPurgeTimeout</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ -> FaultMonitor Momentary report]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>120</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bInPressureBand</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ diagnostic: pressure within purge band]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bOkToPurge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ "OK to purge" drain-phase latch]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>136</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rPressureBandUpper</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rPressureBandLower</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonDrainOpen</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ valve-open dwell]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonEquilibrate</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ valve-closed settle]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>448</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonPurgeTimeout</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ overall watchdog]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>672</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_HmiSetpoints</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 ST_HmiSetpoints
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Direction: Pi -> PLC (request) and PLC -> Pi (applied echo in ST_HmiStatus).
 Pi writes the whole struct, then pulses stCommand.bApplySetpoints.
 FB_Hmi clamps each value to ST_SetpointLimits before applying, and the
 clamped result is echoed in ST_HmiStatus.rSet*Applied so the UI always
 shows the truth, not the request.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>136</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bSetPurgeOnStartup</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetFlow</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ requested flow setpoint      [SLM]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetDsPressure</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ downstream pressure setpoint [Torr]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetSpaTemp</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SPA temperature setpoint     [degC]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetElevation</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ meters above seal level [MASL] ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>104</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>pack_mode</Name><Value>1</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_StateMachine</Name><BitSize>2176</BitSize><SubItem><Name>stProcessValues</Name><Type>ST_ProcessValues</Type><BitSize>368</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stFaults</Name><Type>ST_Faults</Type><BitSize>248</BitSize><BitOffs>400</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stHmiSetpoints</Name><Type>ST_HmiSetpoints</Type><BitSize>136</BitSize><BitOffs>648</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_SystemState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ system state]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>784</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_SystemState.InitController</EnumText></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bControlEnable</Name><Type