ATA[ --- state entry detection (rising edge of a new state) ---]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>896</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bEntry</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE on the first cycle of the current state]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonWarmup</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TC3 warmup, legacy 120 s (V1532)]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>928</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonDiffPress</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ dP settle, legacy 15 min baseline (see rung ~498)]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1152</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonFillTimeout</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonFillStopDelay</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1600</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonPurgeTimeout</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1824</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tWarmupTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ legacy "Begin a 120 sec warm up timer for TC3"]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2048</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#120S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tDiffPressTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ legacy baseline 15 min]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2080</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#15M</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tFillTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2112</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#10M</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tPurgeTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2144</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#10M</DateTime></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>_IsDiffPressEstablished</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TODO: real dP target from setpoints/params (legacy "Purge dP"/INI_SP).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RequestFault</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Force Fault. Called by MAIN when FB_FaultMonitor latches a fault.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RequestStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SES ON. Honored only from SesOff (checked in the CASE).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RequestMaintenance</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Enter Maintenance. Honored only from SesOff.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RequestExitMaint</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_TempsInBand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TODO: real temperature bands from params (Warmup Temp V1535, Max Temp V1522).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RequestFaultReset</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Operator reset. Only leaves Fault when latching faults have cleared.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_FlowInBand</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_IsInitComplete</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TODO: port the final S1 readiness checks (temps settled, dP stable).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_FlowPercent</Name><ReturnType>REAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RequestStop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SES OFF / abort. Honored from any running or startup state.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_IsSpaWarm</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_WaterFillMode</Name><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>Idle</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>StartupFill</Text><Enum>10</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RunningAutofill</Text><Enum>20</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property><Property><Name>strict</Name></Property><Property><Name>to_string</Name></Property><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_WaterFill</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 FB_WaterFill | VERIFIED 7.30.26 DA
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

 TWO modes selected by eMode:

   StartupFill
     - Open SV4 while the filtered CENTER switch (LS1) is dry.
     - The instant LS1 is covered, CLOSE SV4 and run a fixed confirm dwell
       (legacy T24 = 5 s). Valve does NOT keep filling during the dwell.
     - When the dwell completes -> bFillComplete.
     - If the fill-fault timer (legacy T10, preset tFillFaultTime) expires
       while LS1 is still dry -> bWaterFillFault (legacy B1600.15 -> S10).

   RunningAutofill
     - A self-contained PID holds level at the center switch (setpoint 25).
       Its output % is time-proportioned onto the on/off solenoid over
       tFillCycle (legacy T20 / V1516) -> metered trickle to replace boil-off.
     - Lower-duty floor: below rFillMinDuty (legacy 10%) the valve
       stays shut - no meaningless sub-threshold pulsing.
     - If the PID sits pinned at full output longer than tWaterFillCheck -> bWaterRegFault

 Switch filtering: raw center/empty switches debounced with
 symmetric on/off delays (tLevelFilter).

 Drives NO coil directly. Outputs qFillValve; FB_OutputHandler (single
 writer) maps it to GVL_IO

=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>1984</BitSize><SubItem><Name>eMode</Name><Type>E_WaterFillMode</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ StartupFill | RunningAutofill | Idle]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCenterSwitch</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ RAW LS1 center (X2). Filtered internally.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bEmptySwitch</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ RAW LS3 empty  (X4). Filtered internally.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>56</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAutofillEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ legacy X13 autofill-off signal]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>qFillValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ -> FB_OutputHandler -> SV4]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFillComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ startup fill done (LS1 covered + dwell)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWaterFillFault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ startup fill timeout (legacy B1600.15)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCenterFiltered</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ exposed filtered LS1 (HMI / diagnostics)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bEmptyFiltered</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ exposed filtered LS3]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>104</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonCenterOn</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ---- switch debounce (symmetric on/off = tLevelFilter) ----]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonCenterOff</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonEmptyOn</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>576</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonEmptyOff</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>800</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonFillFault</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1024</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonFillDwell</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ fixed confirm (tFillConfirm = 5 s)]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1248</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonAutoFillFault</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ alarm for detecting overfill during auto]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1472</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonAutoFillDwell</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ legacy T63, preset tWaterFillCheck (V1555)]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1696</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAutoFillActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1920</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ePrevMode</Name><Type>E_WaterFillMode</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1936</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bModeEntry</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1952</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_OutputHandler</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 FB_OutputHandler
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 The SINGLE WRITER for every physical output coil (GVL_IO.qx*).
 No other POU may assign a valve or heater output. This eliminates the
 multi-writer races the original ladder was prone to (any rung could drive
 any Y coil).

 SV1..SV4 are fast-acting ON/OFF solenoids: fully open or fully closed,
 never modulated. All valve logic here is therefore boolean. (The PID
 loops in FB_PressureControl drive continuous outputs elsewhere - most
 likely the analog output card - NOT these solenoids.)

 Responsibilities:
   1. Resolve each valve's command from the current context:
        - Maintenance state -> HMI manual overrides (already state-gated)
        - SesOff            -> safe shutdown incl. SV2 pressure relief
        - Fault             -> hard close everything
        - running states    -> automatic requests (fill / purge / delivery)
   2. Enforce hard interlocks that NO state may bypass.
   3. Force heaters off whenever the system is not running.
   4. Publish arValveState for HMI feedback.

 LAST call in MAIN, after the state machine + control FBs produced intent.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>864</BitSize><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_SystemState</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWaterFillValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FB_WaterFill request  -> SV4]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bPurgeValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FB_Purge request      -> SV2 during purge]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>56</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDeliveryPermit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ state machine: SV3 delivery allowed]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtHeaterEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI heater enable]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arValveOverride</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ 1=SV1 2=SV2 3=SV3 4=SV4]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stProcess</Name><Type>ST_ProcessValues</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ --- process feedback needed for actuation timing ---]]></Comment><BitSize>368</BitSize><BitOffs>112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arValveState</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ feedback for HMI (what we actually commanded this cycle)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>480</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHeatersOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>512</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSV1_DrainValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ resolved valve commands before interlocks]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>520</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSV2_SpaValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>528</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSV3_DeliveryValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>536</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSV4_WaterInletValve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>544</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bH1Upstream</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ resolved heater commands]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>552</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bH2Purifier</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>560</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFmHeater</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>568</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtHeater</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>576</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonSv2Close</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SesOff SV2 pressure relief delayed close]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>608</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRunningState</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>832</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_HmiStatus</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 ST_HmiStatus
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 EVERYTHING the RPi HMI displays, packed into ONE struct so pyads can
 refresh the whole UI with a single read:
     plc.read_by_name('GVL_HMI.stStatus', structure_def=ST_HMI_STATUS)

 Direction: PLC -> Pi only. The Pi must never write this struct.
 pack_mode 1: byte-aligned, no padding — pyads structure_def matches 1:1.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>1920</BitSize><SubItem><Name>nPlcHeartbeat</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ increments every PLC cycle group; Pi checks it changes]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nHmiHeartbeatEcho</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last heartbeat value received from Pi (debug aid)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHmiOnline</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ PLC's view: Pi heartbeat is alive]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_SystemState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ current state (INT under the hood)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStateName</Name><Type>STRING(31)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ human-readable, e.g. 'SteamFlowing' (state pill)]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bReady</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ green Ready dot (temps in band, no faults)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>344</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAlarmActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ red Alarm dot (any fault bit set)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nActiveFaults</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ count of active fault bits (Alarms page stat card)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>360</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stProcess</Name><Type>ST_ProcessValues</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ pressures, temps, flow, water level]]></Comment><BitSize>368</BitSize><BitOffs>376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFillComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ water fill complete]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>744</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rFlowPercent</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ rFlowActual / rFlowRated * 100 (bar graph)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>752</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stFaults</Name><Type>ST_Faults</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ process faults]]></Comment><BitSize>248</BitSize><BitOffs>784</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arPidOutput</Name><Type>REAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>6</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ 1 dP, 2 SPA temp, 3 heater, 4 water, 5 FM temp, 6 spare]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>1032</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetFlowApplied</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SL]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetDsPressApplied</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Torr]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetSpaTempApplied</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ degC]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1288</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bMaintModeActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE while eState = Maintenance]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1320</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arValveState</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ SV1 drain, SV2 main, SV3 process, SV4 water]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1328</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLoopbackOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ legacy C31]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1360</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDrainModeOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1368</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sPlcVersion</Name><Type>STRING(31)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ version of the PLC program]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>1376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sHmiVersion</Name><Type>STRING(31)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ echoed from Pi at startup, shown for record]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>1632</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nUptimeSeconds</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1888</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>pack_mode</Name><Value>1</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_HmiCommand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 ST_HmiCommand
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Direction: Pi -> PLC. Consume-on-read pattern:
   * Pi writes TRUE to a command bit (pyads write_by_name).
   * FB_Hmi latches it into its outputs for exactly one PLC cycle,
     then writes FALSE back. The Pi never needs to clear anything.

=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><SubItem><Name>nHmiHeartbeat</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pi increments each poll cycle; never reset]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSesOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ start command]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSesOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ stop command ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFaultReset</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ reset all faults]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFaultAck</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ acknowledge (silences banner, faults stay listed)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>56</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bEnterMaint</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ request Maintenance state]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExitMaint</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ leave Maintenance ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>aValveCmd</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ SV1 drain, SV2 main, SV3 process, SV4 water]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLoopbackOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ legacy C31 loopback mode]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDrainMode</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ drain mode]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>120</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDpControlOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ suspend diff pressure control]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bTempControlOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ suspend purif