me>diJitterMax</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>512</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dwCycleCount</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>544</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>wTaskStatus</Name><Type>WORD</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>576</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>wNumOfJitterDistributions</Name><Type>WORD</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>592</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>pJitterDistribution</Name><Type PointerTo="1">_Implicit_Jitter_Distribution</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>608</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWithinSPSTimeSlicing</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>640</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>byDummy</Name><Type>BYTE</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>648</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bShouldBlock</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>656</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>664</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dwIECCycleCount</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>672</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>signature_flag</Name><Value>256</Value></Property><Property><Name>hide</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_Standard">R_TRIG</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
	Rising Edge detection.
]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><SubItem><Name>CLK</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Signal to detect ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Q</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ rising edge at signal detected ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>M</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>conditionalshow_all_locals</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_PressureControl</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 FB_PressureControl | DRAFT 8.2.26 - NOT YET VERIFIED ON HARDWARE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 All closed-loop heater control. 

 Each loop has two parts:
   PID  -> a demand in percent
   PWM  -> that percent turned into on/off time inside a fixed period

 LOOP MAP:
   [1] Boiler / upstream pressure  PT1 -> H1   PID1
   [2] SPA (purifier) temperature  TC1 -> H2   PID2
   [3] Flow meter temperature      TC2 -> H3   PID3
   [4] External line heater        TC3 -> H4   bang-bang + hysteresis, NOT PID.

 BOILER PRESSURE SETPOINT (loop 1) has three sources, in priority order:
   1. PurgeVessel state -> purge target pressure
   2. SPA not yet flushed -> PT3 + initial dP (100 Torr)
   3. normal -> PT2 + target dP + tuning offset
 In cases 1 and 2 the PWM period is doubled while the max on-time stays
 fixed, which is how the legacy capped the boiler heater at 50 % duty.
 Once flushed, the setpoint is RAMPED at 1 Torr per 0.5 s instead of stepped.
 Drives NO coil directly. Outputs heater demands; FB_OutputHandler is the
 single writer and still gates everything on state.

 DEVIATIONS FROM THE LEGACY (all deliberate, all flagged inline):
   * gains are re-expressed in engineering units (%/Torr, %/degC) - see
     GVL_SysParameters for the conversion arithmetic. RETUNE ON THE BENCH.
   * setpoint ramp clamps at the target instead of dithering +/-1 Torr.
   * ramp is preloaded from live PT1 on enable (legacy did this only on the
     hot-restart path, rung 85).
   * derivative acts on the measurement, not the error, to kill setpoint kick.
   * SPA heater gets a hard over-temperature cut. The legacy had none.
   * external heater gets turn-off hysteresis. The legacy had none.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>2912</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FB_StateMachine.bControlEnable]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_SystemState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ needed to detect PurgeVessel]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDpControlOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI/maint: suspend loop 1]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bTempControlOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI/maint: suspend loop 2]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtHeaterEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI: external heater allowed]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stProcess</Name><Type>ST_ProcessValues</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ scaled PVs]]></Comment><BitSize>368</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stSetpoints</Name><Type>ST_HmiSetpoints</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ operator setpoints, already clamped by FB_Hmi]]></Comment><BitSize>136</BitSize><BitOffs>456</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rTargetDiffPressure</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ [Torr] from FB_FlowCalcs]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>608</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bH1_UpstreamHeater</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ H1]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>640</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bH2_SpaHeater</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ H2]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>648</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bH3_FlowmeterHeater</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ H3]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>656</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bH4_ExternalHeater</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ H4]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>664</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arOutputPct</Name><Type>REAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ loop demand 0..100 %]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>672</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rBoilerSpTarget</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ where we want to be]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>800</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rBoilerSpActive</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ramped SP fed to PID1]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>832</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDiffPressReached</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>864</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rtrigEnable</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">R_TRIG</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ --- edges / gating ----------------------------------------------------]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>896</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bPurging</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>960</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFlushed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>968</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbSampleTick</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ --- PID sample-rate gate (legacy K5 = 0.05 s) -----------------]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>992</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSample</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1216</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rDt</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ [s] sample interval as a real]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1248</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbRampTick</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ --- loop 1 setpoint generation ----------------------------------------]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>1280</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tPwmPeriod1</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1504</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rDutyCap1</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1536</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arIntegral</Name><Type>REAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ --- per-loop PID state (index = legacy PID number) --------------------]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>1568</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arPrevPv</Name><Type>REAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>1696</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arPrimed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1824</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arPwmTimer</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ --- per-loop PWM state -------------------------------------------------]]></Comment><BitSize>896</BitSize><BitOffs>1856</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>arPwmDutyLatched</Name><Type>REAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>2752</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>2880</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>ResetLoop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 ResetLoop
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Clears every piece of memory belonging to one loop: integral accumulator,
 derivative history, PWM timer and latched duty, published output.
 Called when the loop is disabled so a re-enable never inherits wind-up or
 a stale pulse width.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>nLoop</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>RunPid</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 RunPid
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Standard (ISA) positional PID, output in percent.

   out = Kp * e  +  (Kp/Ti) * INTEGRAL(e)  -  Kp * Td * d(PV)/dt

 Derivative acts on the MEASUREMENT, not the error, so a setpoint change
 does not produce a derivative spike.

 Anti-windup: the integral accumulator is clamped to the output range. This
 is the same trick as legacy rung 456 ("freeze integral if over"), which
 clamped the PID bias word to the output maximum.

 State lives in the FB's arrays, indexed by nLoop, so one method serves
 every loop. Call at the sample rate only - it uses rDt, not the task cycle.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><ReturnType>REAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>nLoop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ 1..4, index into the state arrays]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rSp</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ setpoint, engineering units]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rPv</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ process value, same units]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rKp</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ proportional gain [% per engineering unit]]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rTi</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ integral / reset time [s]. 0 disables integral action]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rTd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ derivative / rate time [s]. 0 disables derivative]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rOutMin</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ output floor [%]]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rOutMax</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ output ceiling [%]]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rDt</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ sample interval [s]]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>rError</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rProp</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rDeriv</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rOut</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>RunPwm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 RunPwm
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Time-proportioned output: turns a 0..100 % demand into a digital heater
 command with a fixed period. 

 The demand is LATCHED at each period boundary. Without this the
 on-time would move underneath an in-progress pulse.

 Must be called EVERY task cycle - the period timer only advances when it
 is called. Resolution is one task cycle (10 ms), so a 2 s period gives
 0.5 % granularity.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>nLoop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ 1..4, index into the timer array]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rDutyPct</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ demand 0..100 %]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>tPeriod</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ PWM period]]></Comment><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>nPeriodMs</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>nOnMs</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rDuty</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>MAIN</Name><SubItem><Name Static="true">HMI_bRun</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI Variables]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">reqFillVavle</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">HMI_nPT1</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">eSystemState</Name><Type>E_SystemState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ state machine]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">GVL_Process</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">fbFaultMonitor</Name><Type>FB_FaultMonitor</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ function blocks]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">fbFlowCalcs</Name><Type>FB_FlowCalcs</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">fbHmi</Name><Type>FB_Hmi</Type><BitSize>1504</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">fbPurge</Name><Type>FB_Purge</Type><BitSize>896</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">fbStateMachine</Name><Type>FB_StateMachine</Type><Bi